/* Isolation probe: two mutually recursive predicates and no extra argument.
   Answers in about a second, so a second predicate is not what makes the
   flag-carrying version of this rotation hard -- the extra ARGUMENT is, and
   only when its value changes.  See `..._deadarg_alt_valid.hes`. */
Main 0
s.t.
Main (z:int): bool =mu forall (a:int). forall (b:int). (a = 0 /\ b = 0) \/ L6 a b;
L6 (a:int) (b:int): bool =mu a > 0 /\ b >= 0 \/ L7 a b;
L7 (a:int) (b:int): bool =mu a > 0 /\ b >= 0 \/ L6 (-b) a;
